# Every file is checked out byte-for-byte as committed.  Git must NOT normalise line endings
# here: this package's own 03_code/verify.py hash-checks code and data against
# 00_admin/2026-09-04-shipped-outputs/MANIFEST-outputs.csv, so a single CRLF->LF rewrite changes
# a sha256 and the package fails its own verifier on a fresh clone.  That is not hypothetical:
# 00_admin/2026-09-05-unstable-cells.csv is class exact_hash and contains CRLF.
#
# The shell scripts are stored with LF, so a Windows clone still gets scripts bash can run --
# checking out exactly what was committed is what achieves that, not converting it.
* -text
